      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector",
      "problem": "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(-3,-4,-5)$ and parallel to $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
