    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-69783",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line",
      "problem": "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,0,0)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ Find all the possible points $R$ on that line such that $RP=3\\sqrt{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $R$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩)-⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PR=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RP & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PR}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 3$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{1}}=⟨1,0,0⟩+3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨4,3,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{2}}=⟨1,0,0⟩-3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨-2,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(-2,-3,-3).$",
      "answer_fields": [
